      "sha": "449d90af6e61716a0de4aadd31d457f9bb30643a",
      "author": "DevPrice",
      "summary": "Guard per-frame Keyboard.current and Mouse.current reads against null (#1751)",
      "description": "Keyboard.current and Mouse.current are null when no such device is\nattached: on Xbox, on a PC driven only by a controller, or right after a\nmouse is unplugged. Several Update methods dereferenced them\nunconditionally, so they threw a NullReferenceException every frame in\nthose setups:\n\n- GameManager: Escape to pause and Ctrl+Tab for debug text\n- SongSearchingField: Escape to clear the search\n- MainMenuBackground: camera parallax following the mouse\n- HideCursor: mouse movement re-showing the gameplay cursor\n- PracticePause and PracticeSectionMenu: scroll-wheel adjustment\n\nEach site now treats a missing device as one producing no input, so\nbehavior with a keyboard and mouse is unchanged and no early return\nskips the rest of an Update. The keyboard checks require the device;\nthe practice menus read a scroll delta of zero; MainMenuBackground\nfollows the cursor at a rate of zero, so it still runs its intro camera\nslide and holds the last parallax position.\n\nMouse.current also goes null whenever its current mouse is removed,\nincluding the Input System's VirtualMouse device that a gamepad-driven\nsoftware cursor adds while shown and removes when hidden. While such a\nvirtual mouse is current, these sites treat it like any mouse: the menu\nbackground follows it and its scroll adjusts practice sections. Cursor\nvisibility in HideCursor never depended on a mouse existing, only the\ntimer reset did, and the cursor is always shown while paused.\n\nThe other device reads in YARG code (IdleDimmer,\nPlayerContainer.HasConnectedKeyboardProfile) were already guarded, and\nthere are no Gamepad, Pointer or Touchscreen .current reads or legacy\nUnityEngine.Input calls outside the third-party VLCUnity input shim,\nwhich guards its own.\n\nVerified by compiling Assembly-CSharp with Unity 6000.3.5f2's Roslyn\nusing the standalone IL2CPP player defines (exit code 0) and the WSA\nplayer defines (only the pre-existing FileExplorerHelper CS0103 errors).\nNot run in Unity or on a device without a keyboard or mouse."
    },
